{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-local-cohomology-group","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:local-cohomology-group","kind":"definition","title":"Local cohomology at the unit defect","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-maximal-ideal-defect"],"cites":["references/yekutieli2015","references/yekutieli2010"],"tags":["local-cohomology","defect","H1","derived-functor"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalCohomologyGroup","text":"local-cohomology-group.md","leanSource":"local-cohomology-group.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:local-cohomology-group\"></a><p>The <strong>local cohomology group</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^1_{\\mathfrak{m}_1}(A) = R^1\\Gamma_{\\mathfrak{m}_1}(A)</code> measures the algebraic obstruction to extending sections across the defect at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = 1</code>. In this non-commutative setting, the derived category framework generalizes the commutative concept of principal parts supported at the singularity.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/local-cohomology-group.md","heading":"Definition","number":"8.13.3","page":"b/def-local-cohomology-group","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalCohomologyGroup","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/local-cohomology-group.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
